#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# asech

#% text
# `asech(z)` gives the inverse hyperbolic secant.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For complex `z` the principal value is `acosh(1/z)`.

#% item
# Exact special values are applied; other exact arguments stay unevaluated. The function is not odd: `asech(-x)` stays as it is.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
asech(1)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
asech(0.5)
#% output
#= 1.3169578969248166

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
asech(2.0)
#% output
#= -1.1102230246251565e-16 + 1.0471975511965976im

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(asech(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= 1.7627471740390860504652186499595846

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `atan`, `asin`, `acos`
